================================================================================
## Lakebase graph engine rejects a bare branch name ("production")
================================================================================

Context:
The deployment docs and deploy.config.sh configure LAKEBASE_BRANCH as a bare
branch id ("production"). The Settings > Lakebase Connection tab pre-fills an
empty branch field from that env var, so saving before the branch picker
loads (or saving through the Advanced JSON) stores
graph_engine_config.lakebase.lakebase_branch = "production" next to
lakebase_project = "projects/<p>". GraphDBFactory, the Lakebase health check
and the graph DB setup path passed that value straight to
BranchLakebaseAuth, which expects "projects/<p>/branches/<b>", so the health
check showed "Health check failed" and the graph backend was unavailable.
Seen on two fresh deployments; the same code exists in 0.8.1.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/engine_config.py
   New resolve_lakebase_branch_path(): returns a full branch path; a bare
   branch is joined with lakebase_project ("projects/" prefix added when the
   project is a bare id); unchanged when no project is set.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py
   Lakebase backend resolves the branch through resolve_lakebase_branch_path.
3. src/back/objects/domain/settings/graphengine/GraphEngineLakebaseSettings.py
   Health check and the graph DB setup / objects / permissions auth path
   resolve the branch (form value or saved value) the same way.
4. tests/units/graphdb/test_graph_engine_config_keys.py
   Tests for full path, bare branch + project path, bare branch + bare
   project id, bare branch without project, and unset branch.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/graphdb/engine_config.py
- src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py
- src/back/objects/domain/settings/graphengine/GraphEngineLakebaseSettings.py
- tests/units/graphdb/test_graph_engine_config_keys.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_lgit_2026-10-27.log

